      "updated_at": "2025-12-23T18:30:18Z",
      "body": "It's pretty atypical for Python APIs to not provide a clean, recoverable, error for malformed arguments. Is there a reason for fcntl to diverge from this? It doesn't appear to be documented that it can raise SystemError at all.",
